      "extract": "As pointed out in the introduction, the full system of equations for ﬁnding a hyperbolic structure on a triangulation fails to have rank equal to the number of variables in both the ﬁnite and ideal case. Thus, veriﬁcation by interval methods in the ideal case also relies on a theorem showing that if a suitable subsystem is fulﬁlled, all equations are fulﬁlled. Unfortunately, the paper [HIK+16] did not cite this",
